Subject: [PATCH 03/11] feat(pqc-m3): state.db device_identities gets 4
 ML-DSA-65 columns (additive)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PQC migration (whitepaper 2.1.3 + 2.2.1): the device_identities table gains
4 nullable columns for the future wrap envelope path. The change is purely
additive — no schema-version bump, no downgraded-build impact (AGENTS.md
schema-additive rule).

  mldsa_public_key_pem         TEXT    -- new ML-DSA-65 wire format
  mldsa_private_key_pem        TEXT    -- new ML-DSA-65 wire format
  mldsa_private_key_wrapped    BLOB    -- M4/M5 AES-256-GCM envelope
  mldsa_private_key_wrap_key_id TEXT   -- active keyring key id

- src/state/openclaw-state-schema.sql: device_identities CREATE TABLE now
  declares the 4 new columns. Other tables in the schema are untouched.
- src/state/openclaw-state-db-schema-additive.ts: 4 ensureColumn calls
  added to ensureAdditiveStateColumns so a pre-M3 fork upgrades in place.
- src/state/openclaw-state-db.generated.d.ts: DeviceIdentities interface
  gains the 4 nullable fields (BLOB typed as Uint8Array | null per
  whitepaper 3.1 — NOT Buffer | null, see TS narrowing gotcha).
- src/state/openclaw-state-db-schema-additive.test.ts: 4 invariants —
  additive on fresh db, idempotent re-runs, pre-M3 row stays readable with
  NULL mldsa_* columns, fresh ML-DSA-65 row round-trips through the new
  columns including the BLOB envelope shape.

M3 store behavior is unchanged: the existing public_key_pem / private_key_pem
columns continue to receive the ML-DSA-65 prefixed base64url wire format from
M2. M5 will route writes through the mldsa_* columns and add the wrap
envelope.

